 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\nYou can only extrapolate from a previous period, if it is representative. Whether a period is representative or not is a result of the\noriginal weighting procedure.\n\nDetermining Whether a Period is Representative\nWhether a base period is representative or not is determined as follows:\nWeighting portion of period = Minimum portion\nor\nMinimum portion in percent * Length of meter reading period\n= Minimum length of base period\n\n\u00abSe Example\n\ne The following meter reading reasons exist:\n\ne O1 Periodic meter reading\n\ne 03 Final meter reading\n\ne O6 Meter reading at move-in (M)\n\ne O8 Meter reading at installation (I)\n\ne 09 Interim meter reading without billing (Y)\ne O2 Interim meter reading with billing (Z)\n\ne 10 Control meter reading\ne The period length of the portion is 1 year (365 days)\ne The minimum portion defined in the rate is 50%\n\ne The minimum requirements to determine whether the base period is representative are determined in the following\nway:\n\nWeighting portion of period = Minimum portion\n\nor\n\nMinimum portion in percent (50%) * Length of meter reading period (365 days)\n= Minimum length of base period (182.5 days)\n\nIn the example, the base period must have a minimum weighting portion of 50% or be at least 182.5 days long in order to be\n\nrepresentative.\n",
